; Cow — AnimalDefinition data entry (gdd.md -> Data Schemas / Content Architecture).
; Roster row: roster.md -> Already-Defined Roster | Ruled: decisions.md -> D-43.
; Asset: Quaternius "Ultimate Animated Animal Pack", CC0 1.0 Universal — see
;   project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres.
; Source: source-content/assets/Ultimate Animated Animals - July 2021/glTF/Cow.gltf
;
; SPECIES: domestic cattle (Bos taurus). Same real species as Bull — no ecological basis
; to split habitat axes, so Cow and Bull share identical habitat_needs/personality/
; farm_tolerant by design (D-43); they already share a base mesh in the imported asset
; (content-pipeline-status.md's flagged shared-mesh risk), and the human ruled 2026-07-26
; to keep both as separate roster spots regardless.
;
; CAPACITY FIELDS (D-43): capacity_radius = 0 -> SENTINEL `CAPACITY_RADIUS_FOLLOWS_SCOUT`,
; meaning "equal to scout_radius" (8), not a radius of zero. tiles_per_individual = 5
; (vs. Bull's 6 — a bull kept singly needs more room than a cow in a herd; explicitly
; acknowledged in D-43 as the thin, one-number-only distinction between the two).
; max_individuals = 6. Farm-tolerant.
;
; fact_text is docs/content/cleared-pool-fact-cards.md § Cow's CORRECTED proposed line,
; transcribed verbatim — all four checklist steps PASS there. This replaced an earlier
; draft naming Holstein black-and-white spots, which a 2026-08-06 consistency-check pass
; found did not match the imported Cow.gltf's materials (solid brown/tan, no black or
; white body material, no pattern texture) — see the source file's full correction note.
;   "coat can come in many colors — black, white, reddish brown, or brown" -> ADW Bos
;   taurus, "Physical Description": "The body is covered in short hair, the color of which
;   varies from black through white, reddish brown, and brown."
; https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Bos_taurus/
;
; news_reports intentionally empty — News Report pools for this pool are a separate, later
; purchase (not part of Content Pipeline step 4/5 for this dispatch).
;
; TIERS — RE-SPEC 2026-09-04 (habitat tiers).
;
; PROPOSAL, NOT A DECISION. Every divisor, radius and cap below is this design's own
; first-pass proposal awaiting human sign-off, per the project rule that all tuning values
; are the human's. Source: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-habitat-tiers-design.md § 9.
;
; THIS IS WHAT FIXES THE DEFECT this whole design exists for: Cow used to share the
; IDENTICAL `open_grass, cultivated` recipe with Horse, Bull and Alpaca (see § 1 of the
; spec), so one pasture attracted all four at once. Cow now gates on `barn*` AND `silo*` —
; a real farmstead, not just grass — which no other species' tiers require together.
;
; TWO TIERS: "pair" (`barn*` `silo*` `open_grass/5`) and "herd" (the same gates plus
; `water/3`, arriving in pairs) — a barn and a silo get a couple; adding water for the herd
; to drink from is what grows it.
;
; The legacy flat fields (habitat_needs / tiles_per_individual / max_individuals) are LEFT
; IN PLACE and are now inert: `effective_tiers()` prefers `tiers` when non-empty. They are
; retained so a rollback is a one-line edit rather than a re-authoring.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="AnimalDefinition" load_steps=15 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/animal_definition.gd" id="1_schema"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/animals/cow/Cow.tscn" id="2_model"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_need.gd" id="3_need"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_tier.gd" id="4_tier"]

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_pair_barn"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "barn"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_pair_silo"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "silo"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_pair_grass"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "open_grass"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 5

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="tier_pair"]
script = ExtResource("4_tier")
id = "pair"
needs = Array[Resource]([SubResource("need_pair_barn"), SubResource("need_pair_silo"), SubResource("need_pair_grass")])
limits = Array[Resource]([])
max_individuals = 2
arrival_group_size = 1

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_herd_barn"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "barn"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_herd_silo"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "silo"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_herd_grass"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "open_grass"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 5

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_herd_water"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "water"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 3

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="tier_herd"]
script = ExtResource("4_tier")
id = "herd"
needs = Array[Resource]([SubResource("need_herd_barn"), SubResource("need_herd_silo"), SubResource("need_herd_grass"), SubResource("need_herd_water")])
limits = Array[Resource]([])
max_individuals = 6
arrival_group_size = 2

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_schema")
id = "cow"
display_name = "Cow"
habitat_needs = Array[String](["cultivated", "open_grass"])
personality = "Bold"
avoids = Array[String]([])
farm_tolerant = true
scout_radius = 8
capacity_radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 5
max_individuals = 6
tiers = Array[Resource]([SubResource("tier_pair"), SubResource("tier_herd")])
emits_tags = Array[String]([])
model_scenes = Array[PackedScene]([ExtResource("2_model")])
fact_text_pool = Array[String](["A cow's short coat can come in many colors — black, white, reddish brown, or brown — so no two cows have to match."])
news_reports = Array[String]([])
